WEBVTT

00:00:01.730 --> 00:00:04.940
So, everyone's okay with us making
this our base for now, right?

00:00:05.740 --> 00:00:08.150
It's a small room with four 
beds and nothing else,

00:00:08.720 --> 00:00:11.400
but this cheap inn is where
 we'll make our start!

00:00:11.840 --> 00:00:14.660
The place where the legend 
of the Crimson Vow begins!

00:00:19.230 --> 00:00:22.080
The first thing we need is a stable income.

00:00:22.600 --> 00:00:25.320
We need money for food and 
weapons and things, after all.

00:00:25.810 --> 00:00:29.590
For now, we need about 
ten gold coins a month.

00:00:29.590 --> 00:00:32.970
That's another reason we have to go out 
and tear through those Hunter quests.

00:00:33.160 --> 00:00:35.040
Doing that will get us out of this cheap hotel,

00:00:35.040 --> 00:00:37.850
and to a much bigger inn with a bath!

00:00:37.850 --> 00:00:39.020
What?

00:00:39.020 --> 00:00:42.100
This place might be cheap, 
but it's nice, you know.

00:00:42.100 --> 00:00:44.770
Though, the rooms are a little old,
 the toilet is shared,

00:00:45.290 --> 00:00:49.020
and the walls are thin so you can 
hear what's going on next door.

00:00:49.320 --> 00:00:53.280
Well, you can't expect more. It's nice, 
but it is a cheap inn, after all.

00:00:53.460 --> 00:00:56.950
Indeed. It's a nice place, 
but it is a cheap inn.

00:00:58.240 --> 00:01:00.870
Stop calling our place a cheap inn!

00:01:01.110 --> 00:01:03.750
If you'd be quiet and listen, 
you'd see how horrible you sound!

00:01:04.320 --> 00:01:06.880
Besides which, you said you had 
no money and nowhere to go,

00:01:06.880 --> 00:01:09.900
so I charged you even less!

00:01:10.730 --> 00:01:12.970
You could show a little gratitude!

00:01:12.970 --> 00:01:15.050
Yes, ma'am. We're very sorry.

00:01:15.570 --> 00:01:17.160
Which is why...

00:01:17.160 --> 00:01:20.010
Young ladies, it's time 
to show what you've got!

00:01:20.010 --> 00:01:20.960
Huh?

00:01:25.800 --> 00:01:27.730
Thank you for waiting!

00:01:28.200 --> 00:01:30.870
Your roasted orc with mandragora!

00:01:30.870 --> 00:01:32.480
Oh. Thanks.

00:01:32.680 --> 00:01:35.910
Make it more delicious! 
Make it more delicious!

00:01:35.910 --> 00:01:38.230
Moe! Moe! Kyun!

00:01:42.430 --> 00:01:44.930
We're supposed to do that, too?

00:01:44.930 --> 00:01:46.950
What does, "Moe! Moe!" mean?

00:01:46.950 --> 00:01:47.960
No idea...

00:01:49.740 --> 00:01:52.380
<i>I was right!</i>

00:01:52.620 --> 00:01:55.560
<i>I'm glad I had the girls come here.</i>

00:01:56.570 --> 00:01:58.710
Moe! Moe! Kyun!

00:01:59.200 --> 00:02:00.160
My goodness.

00:02:00.160 --> 00:02:03.680
Making a living sure is 
difficult, isn't it, Mile-sama?

00:02:03.680 --> 00:02:07.410
<i>To think I'd come to another world 
and be forced to work in a maid café...</i>

00:03:35.810 --> 00:03:38.030
Didn't I Say to Make My Abilities 
Average in the Next Life?!

00:03:38.900 --> 00:03:43.030
<b>Episode 4</b>

00:03:38.900 --> 00:03:43.030
<b>Didn't I Say This Was the Crimson Vow's First Step?!</b>

00:03:45.080 --> 00:03:48.790
This is the Hunters' Guild in the Kingdom of Tils.

00:03:51.660 --> 00:03:53.540
Do you see any good quests?

00:03:54.790 --> 00:03:57.040
None of them really feel right.

00:03:57.200 --> 00:03:59.160
Orcs are too easy.

00:03:59.160 --> 00:04:01.840
And we don't have enough 
people to hunt kobolds.

00:04:01.840 --> 00:04:04.050
We can't settle for just any old quest!

00:04:04.430 --> 00:04:08.060
After all, this will be the 
Crimson Vow's first job!

00:04:08.270 --> 00:04:09.640
Hey, what about this one?

00:04:09.920 --> 00:04:12.130
Collecting rock lizard materials.

00:04:12.130 --> 00:04:14.900
Each lizard gets us fifteen small gold coins.

00:04:15.260 --> 00:04:17.080
That's a nice reward!

00:04:17.080 --> 00:04:19.990
And it's a quest that 
C-rank Hunters can handle.

00:04:19.990 --> 00:04:21.210
It's decided!

00:04:21.210 --> 00:04:21.900
Huh?

00:04:22.350 --> 00:04:24.340
The Crimson Vow's first quest...

00:04:24.880 --> 00:04:25.660
That's it!

00:04:32.410 --> 00:04:34.250
Hang on! No one said anything about this!

00:04:34.530 --> 00:04:35.670
Rock lizards are...

00:04:35.870 --> 00:04:38.050
They're huge!

00:04:38.050 --> 00:04:39.670
And they run fast!

00:04:40.250 --> 00:04:45.050
I can beat it with fire magic, but burning 
it to a crisp won't let us fulfill the quest!

00:04:45.050 --> 00:04:46.890
This is quite a problem!

00:04:49.170 --> 00:04:50.720
Running won't accomplish anything!

00:04:51.220 --> 00:04:52.930
Leave this to me!

00:05:12.640 --> 00:05:14.020
Mavis...

00:05:14.020 --> 00:05:16.380
She made it angry.

00:05:17.040 --> 00:05:19.100
We have to do something!

00:05:19.680 --> 00:05:20.660
Oh, I know!

00:05:20.660 --> 00:05:22.370
Reina-san. Pauline-san.

00:05:30.380 --> 00:05:31.180
Uh-oh...

00:05:34.190 --> 00:05:36.520
No one told me it could stand, too!

00:05:39.090 --> 00:05:39.730
Huh?

00:05:44.110 --> 00:05:45.900
I-It's freezing.

00:05:45.900 --> 00:05:47.700
Perfect Freeze!

00:05:47.880 --> 00:05:49.820
Ultra Freeze!

00:05:57.990 --> 00:06:00.040
Mavis-san! Now!

00:06:00.290 --> 00:06:01.300
Mile!

00:06:09.320 --> 00:06:10.380
Got it.

00:06:11.200 --> 00:06:12.100
But it's freezing!

00:06:12.330 --> 00:06:14.600
Mavis-san! Well done!

00:06:14.600 --> 00:06:20.280
But why did ice magic make 
the rock lizard stop?

00:06:20.280 --> 00:06:22.650
Oh. That's simple.

00:06:22.650 --> 00:06:25.480
We made use of a characteristic 
of cold-blooded animals.

00:06:25.890 --> 00:06:28.560
Lizards, reptiles in general, 
and other poikilotherms'

00:06:28.560 --> 00:06:31.460
internal temperatures change according 
to the external temperature.

00:06:31.960 --> 00:06:37.000
That's why, if you use ice magic to suddenly 
lower the temperature, they stop moving.

00:06:37.400 --> 00:06:40.120
Really? Mile-chan, you're so knowledgeable!

00:06:40.570 --> 00:06:43.000
Where did you learn to fight like this?

00:06:43.360 --> 00:06:46.230
"Perfect Freeze," "Ultra Freeze"...

00:06:46.230 --> 00:06:48.360
You even told us what the spells were called.

00:06:48.360 --> 00:06:49.780
What do the names mean?

00:06:49.780 --> 00:06:50.620
Huh?

00:06:50.620 --> 00:06:52.300
Uh... well...

00:06:53.980 --> 00:06:54.580
Hup!

00:06:56.280 --> 00:06:58.480
Ultra Freeze!

00:07:03.970 --> 00:07:06.020
I-It's a secret family technique...

00:07:06.220 --> 00:07:09.860
Well, names aside, I understand the logic.

00:07:11.810 --> 00:07:12.910
At any rate...

00:07:13.170 --> 00:07:16.330
Capture of one rock lizard! Success!

00:07:16.330 --> 00:07:17.600
It's wonderful!

00:07:17.600 --> 00:07:19.020
We did it!

00:07:19.020 --> 00:07:21.540
This is the first step for the Crimson Vow!

00:07:23.790 --> 00:07:26.250
Ten small gold coins, I think.

00:07:26.760 --> 00:07:27.460
Huh?

00:07:27.670 --> 00:07:32.890
B-B-But I'm sure that the request from the 
Abbott Company said fifteen small gold coins.

00:07:32.890 --> 00:07:35.580
That's if it were in perfect condition.

00:07:36.070 --> 00:07:37.600
But, you see?

00:07:37.810 --> 00:07:40.740
On the neck. There's a sword wound.

00:07:41.540 --> 00:07:45.000
Besides which, it's been more than three 
days since you caught it, correct?

00:07:45.000 --> 00:07:47.510
It's degraded over that time.

00:07:47.510 --> 00:07:48.790
A sword wound?

00:07:48.790 --> 00:07:50.990
We had to fight it to capture it,
 so that's just a matter of course!

00:07:51.470 --> 00:07:54.820
Plus, the neck will get cut when 
you break it down anyway!

00:07:55.170 --> 00:07:59.110
And as far as time goes, it's only been a 
little over two days since we caught it.

00:07:59.110 --> 00:08:00.700
Even so...

00:08:01.360 --> 00:08:04.210
Those are our standards, you see.

00:08:04.780 --> 00:08:06.210
Oh, but...

00:08:08.020 --> 00:08:12.210
<i>There's no way these little novice Hunter girls
 can possibly know the value of things yet.</i>

00:08:12.210 --> 00:08:16.220
<i>As I'm a veteran merchant, I'll wheedle
 them down to a bargain price.</i>

00:08:16.790 --> 00:08:18.080
All right.

00:08:18.080 --> 00:08:18.720
Huh?

00:08:19.120 --> 00:08:21.230
Wha... Pauline-san?

00:08:21.390 --> 00:08:24.640
I suppose there's no helping it,
 if you put it like that.

00:08:24.640 --> 00:08:26.150
Yes, exactly!

00:08:26.150 --> 00:08:28.690
Now, I won't treat you 
badly, so just do as I—

00:08:28.690 --> 00:08:29.460
Mile...

00:08:29.460 --> 00:08:31.530
Please put the rock lizard back in storage.

00:08:31.530 --> 00:08:32.480
Huh?

00:08:32.480 --> 00:08:35.360
It seems the materials weren't 
in the desired condition,

00:08:35.360 --> 00:08:38.450
so this quest was a failure. Right?

00:08:38.450 --> 00:08:40.510
Well, if you'll excuse us.

00:08:40.900 --> 00:08:44.040
W-Wait! I never said I 
wouldn't buy it from you!

00:08:44.280 --> 00:08:48.720
Oh, no. Supplying damaged goods 
only worth ten small gold coins

00:08:48.720 --> 00:08:50.670
would bring shame on our party.

00:08:50.840 --> 00:08:52.510
Oh... but... I mean...

00:08:52.990 --> 00:08:54.880
But it really is such a shame.

00:08:54.880 --> 00:08:58.640
We went through all that trouble to catch 
so many, and it was all for nothing.

00:08:58.870 --> 00:09:00.470
Right, Mile?

00:09:00.470 --> 00:09:02.030
Huh? Oh! Yes.

00:09:03.200 --> 00:09:05.900
Rock lizard!

00:09:05.900 --> 00:09:06.850
Huh?

00:09:08.500 --> 00:09:09.000
Huh?

00:09:09.470 --> 00:09:09.860
Huh?

00:09:10.200 --> 00:09:11.820
What?

00:09:12.360 --> 00:09:15.280
With this many, we'll be rolling in mon—

00:09:15.640 --> 00:09:18.330
Fortunately, we hadn't entered 
into an agreement yet.

00:09:19.660 --> 00:09:22.320
Oh! About the two small gold coin 
penalty for breach of contract...

00:09:22.320 --> 00:09:24.800
We've made sure to leave 
it with the Hunters' Guild.

00:09:24.800 --> 00:09:25.870
Please don't worry.

00:09:26.130 --> 00:09:28.210
Oh! Oh, but...!

00:09:29.990 --> 00:09:34.460
<i>You should regret your decision to pick 
a fight with the daughter of merchants.</i>

00:09:37.350 --> 00:09:39.930
<i>Pauline-san... is terrifying!</i>

00:09:40.800 --> 00:09:41.930
I'm glad it worked out, though...

00:09:42.390 --> 00:09:47.260
That the quest itself was invalid, 
so it wasn't a failure on our part.

00:09:47.260 --> 00:09:48.720
Of course not.

00:09:48.720 --> 00:09:52.320
It was the client who didn't stick 
to the facts laid out in the request.

00:09:52.810 --> 00:09:54.760
What do you mean, "ten small gold coins"?

00:09:54.760 --> 00:09:56.990
He was underestimating us
 just because we're new!

00:09:57.190 --> 00:09:58.340
Now, now.

00:09:58.340 --> 00:10:04.080
The Hunters' Guild bought all our rock 
lizards at a fair price, after all...

00:10:04.080 --> 00:10:07.300
And trust in that cheating 
merchant has plummeted.

00:10:07.300 --> 00:10:09.550
Everything is going just as I planned.

00:10:13.040 --> 00:10:16.840
Anyway! We just need to keep it 
up and charge ahead tomorrow!

00:10:26.760 --> 00:10:28.730
Carelessness is the greatest enemy, Mavis.

00:10:32.860 --> 00:10:33.930
Thanks.

00:10:34.320 --> 00:10:34.980
Not at all.

00:10:37.230 --> 00:10:37.650
There!

00:10:43.960 --> 00:10:47.450
Rain, rain! Fall, fall! I'm so happy!

00:10:47.760 --> 00:10:51.460
Mom is coming to pick me 
up with a paper umbrella.

00:10:51.460 --> 00:10:53.450
Where is that song from?

00:10:51.460 --> 00:10:53.960
Drip, drop! Splash, splash! So much fun!

00:10:53.960 --> 00:10:56.840
Oh, it's just... A secret family technique!

00:10:57.060 --> 00:11:01.920
That aside, our work was 
perfect yesterday, wasn't it?

00:11:01.920 --> 00:11:05.780
It could be that we're stronger 
than we think we are.

00:11:05.780 --> 00:11:08.660
We might really be able to 
become legendary Hunters.

00:11:08.660 --> 00:11:09.560
Maybe.

00:11:10.360 --> 00:11:12.790
I'm fine with being a normal Hunter.

00:11:12.790 --> 00:11:14.770
<i>No matter how you look at it, Mile is...</i>

00:11:14.770 --> 00:11:16.940
<i>...probably not ever going to be normal.</i>

00:11:17.390 --> 00:11:19.640
You're all still too naïve.

00:11:19.640 --> 00:11:20.440
Huh?

00:11:20.880 --> 00:11:22.800
If you're satisfied with 
this level of accomplishment,

00:11:22.800 --> 00:11:25.660
forget legendary! Even A rank
 will just be a dream!

00:11:26.210 --> 00:11:28.650
We have to complete even 
more difficult quests,

00:11:28.650 --> 00:11:30.410
so we can level up!

00:11:31.000 --> 00:11:32.460
Level up?

00:11:32.460 --> 00:11:33.170
Us?

00:11:33.360 --> 00:11:34.230
That's right!

00:11:34.230 --> 00:11:37.300
Picking our next quest 
with that point in mind...

00:11:41.470 --> 00:11:42.420
Reina?

00:11:43.070 --> 00:11:44.430
This is...

00:11:44.600 --> 00:11:46.930
A request to guard merchants.

00:11:55.980 --> 00:11:58.650
Somehow, I just can't get 
into my usual rhythm...

00:11:58.810 --> 00:12:04.260
I never imagined cute girls like you 
would be the Hunters to guard us.

00:12:04.260 --> 00:12:06.570
Oh my! You think we're cute?

00:12:06.570 --> 00:12:10.500
Please rest easy. In spite of 
our looks, we're C-rank Hunters.

00:12:11.010 --> 00:12:11.680
Right?

00:12:11.680 --> 00:12:12.220
Huh?

00:12:12.680 --> 00:12:14.900
Y-Yes, we are.

00:12:19.060 --> 00:12:21.630
<i>You mean... guarding merchants?</i>

00:12:21.840 --> 00:12:22.550
Yes.

00:12:23.020 --> 00:12:25.010
Lately, on the main roads to Amroth,

00:12:25.360 --> 00:12:28.060
robbers have been appearing more frequently.

00:12:28.060 --> 00:12:30.000
And among them are those 
who don't think ahead.

00:12:30.000 --> 00:12:33.630
They kill merchants, Hunters, 
everyone. They're truly horrible.

00:12:36.030 --> 00:12:38.820
What you're saying is that 
we'll be facing people.

00:12:39.200 --> 00:12:43.020
Which is why I don't recommend 
this for novices like yourselves.

00:12:43.020 --> 00:12:44.020
That quest!

00:12:45.060 --> 00:12:46.010
We'll do it!

00:12:49.420 --> 00:12:50.610
<i>Reina-san...</i>

00:12:52.070 --> 00:12:53.560
You've been staring a while. What is it?

00:12:53.560 --> 00:12:56.460
Is my profile really so unusual?

00:12:56.460 --> 00:12:58.470
Oh, no. It's not that.

00:12:59.190 --> 00:13:01.210
I know I'm being selfish.

00:13:01.690 --> 00:13:06.100
I just went ahead and accepted this 
quest without really asking any of you.

00:13:06.720 --> 00:13:09.350
I can't deny that it was a sudden decision.

00:13:09.570 --> 00:13:13.770
But I do believe that this 
quest will help us level up.

00:13:14.120 --> 00:13:17.350
And, well, if you really 
want to do it, Reina,

00:13:17.350 --> 00:13:19.150
then it's up to us as 
friends to see it through.

00:13:19.890 --> 00:13:21.090
You two...

00:13:23.600 --> 00:13:25.440
Right? After all...

00:13:25.440 --> 00:13:28.910
We are bound together, 
the Crimson Vow. Right?

00:13:28.910 --> 00:13:32.370
Hey! Why'd you say that when 
I was thinking of saying it?

00:13:46.570 --> 00:13:47.870
Ta-dah!

00:13:48.400 --> 00:13:50.720
They say to prepare for the worst 
and you'll never be sorry!

00:13:51.100 --> 00:13:54.350
I thought this might happen, 
so I brought my old clothes.

00:13:54.930 --> 00:13:56.430
Right, Reina-san?

00:13:59.770 --> 00:14:01.820
Why do you have clothes like these?

00:14:02.010 --> 00:14:05.540
Now, now. It's only while 
our clothes are drying.

00:14:05.540 --> 00:14:08.070
Honestly. Fine, then.

00:14:14.740 --> 00:14:16.060
Um, Mile...

00:14:17.050 --> 00:14:19.860
Why am I in a guy's uniform?

00:14:19.860 --> 00:14:21.880
It was the same at the 
restaurant too, wasn't it?

00:14:22.120 --> 00:14:24.220
It's because girls who like 
Takarazuka requested Mavis-san—

00:14:24.220 --> 00:14:25.240
I mean...

00:14:25.240 --> 00:14:26.900
It's because your frame is larger.

00:14:27.290 --> 00:14:31.180
I thought this might happen. 
I'm glad I brought a guy's uniform, too.

00:14:31.380 --> 00:14:33.760
Oh, just do as you please...

00:14:33.760 --> 00:14:36.040
Oops! I forgot my sword.

00:14:36.040 --> 00:14:38.120
You girls are quite cheerful.

00:14:38.900 --> 00:14:43.570
When I look at you, it makes 
me think of my granddaughter.

00:14:43.870 --> 00:14:45.030
Granddaughter?

00:14:45.030 --> 00:14:49.790
Yes. She's a cute girl, just like you.

00:14:51.360 --> 00:14:56.290
It's a dangerous job, but someone 
has to transport these goods.

00:14:56.540 --> 00:15:02.170
I applied for this job prepared 
to die at any time, but...

00:15:03.600 --> 00:15:06.440
You've shown me something good.

00:15:06.440 --> 00:15:07.780
We won't let you die.

00:15:08.860 --> 00:15:11.560
I'm sorry. I know you're resolved,

00:15:11.560 --> 00:15:14.890
but as long as there's breath in 
my body, I won't let you die.

00:15:15.520 --> 00:15:16.920
Reina-san...

00:15:16.920 --> 00:15:18.390
Excuse me...

00:15:27.090 --> 00:15:29.780
Mile-chan... This size doesn't really...

00:15:30.040 --> 00:15:33.590
I'm sorry! They're mine, 
so they're a little small...

00:15:34.920 --> 00:15:36.670
W-Wait!

00:15:36.670 --> 00:15:39.680
You look just like my granddaughter!

00:15:39.680 --> 00:15:42.410
I can die happy!

00:15:43.870 --> 00:15:46.640
What are you making Pauline wear?

00:15:46.640 --> 00:15:49.420
Sorry! I didn't think the 
reaction would be this positive!

00:15:49.840 --> 00:15:51.700
Um... Mile-sama.

00:15:51.700 --> 00:15:54.990
Isn't it about time to use some search magic?

00:15:54.990 --> 00:15:57.810
Oh man! I totally forgot!

00:16:08.310 --> 00:16:09.280
Lattice Energy Barrier!

00:16:16.640 --> 00:16:19.950
Tch. We've got someone here 
who uses some weird magic.

00:16:21.780 --> 00:16:24.210
What's this? You guys are Hunters?

00:16:24.430 --> 00:16:27.380
I thought you were rich 
students from somewhere.

00:16:27.660 --> 00:16:29.210
I'll thank you not to look down on us.

00:16:29.490 --> 00:16:30.810
We'll leave that, then.

00:16:30.810 --> 00:16:35.720
Against this many, all you 
can do is surrender, right?

00:16:36.100 --> 00:16:39.430
So! Just leave everything you've got,

00:16:39.430 --> 00:16:41.310
and we'll let you keep your lives.

00:16:41.670 --> 00:16:43.640
We know you're just going to kill everyone!

00:16:43.930 --> 00:16:45.810
Not gonna listen, huh?

00:16:46.800 --> 00:16:49.190
Then we'll take it by force!

00:16:52.200 --> 00:16:54.610
The Crimson Vow's first real 
battle against other people!

00:16:54.610 --> 00:16:55.530
Let's go!

00:16:55.730 --> 00:16:56.520
Got it!

00:16:57.170 --> 00:16:59.950
Everyone! Please just 
wait here and don't move.

00:17:00.580 --> 00:17:01.290
Hup!

00:17:01.500 --> 00:17:03.060
Godspeed Sword!

00:17:05.620 --> 00:17:07.210
Water Cutter!

00:17:09.170 --> 00:17:10.880
Fire Ball!

00:17:17.510 --> 00:17:19.850
How can they be so useless 
against little girls?

00:17:19.850 --> 00:17:21.480
Hey! Bring it out!

00:17:21.480 --> 00:17:23.060
Time to show 'em our secret weapon!

00:17:24.140 --> 00:17:25.560
Leave it to me.

00:17:27.290 --> 00:17:31.730
Come, my slaves!

00:17:41.660 --> 00:17:42.240
What?

00:17:43.800 --> 00:17:44.700
This is...!

00:17:46.090 --> 00:17:46.960
It couldn't be!

00:17:49.580 --> 00:17:51.590
Ka-boom!

00:17:52.340 --> 00:17:55.380
There it is! He did a Build Up!

00:17:56.850 --> 00:18:01.430
This is it! The ultimate mystery of 
my magic. My greatest secret weapon!

00:18:01.590 --> 00:18:04.980
My amalgamate rock golem, KaBoom!

00:18:05.350 --> 00:18:07.040
You got me!

00:18:07.040 --> 00:18:09.330
Stretching out an arm! Stretching out a leg!

00:18:09.330 --> 00:18:10.680
Going crash, bang, boom!

00:18:10.680 --> 00:18:13.070
I wanted to do that!

00:18:13.360 --> 00:18:15.860
We do not fear rock golems!

00:18:16.160 --> 00:18:18.070
We already know their weaknesses!

00:18:18.350 --> 00:18:20.900
There!

00:18:23.770 --> 00:18:25.410
The attack didn't work?

00:18:25.680 --> 00:18:29.410
Don't go thinking this is 
like those other rock golems.

00:18:29.410 --> 00:18:34.170
KaBoom's joints have been 
perfectly reinforced with magic.

00:18:34.170 --> 00:18:36.380
Now, it's our turn!

00:18:36.380 --> 00:18:39.240
Go, KaBoom!

00:18:41.780 --> 00:18:44.220
No way! Is he using his "Knuckle" attack?

00:18:47.560 --> 00:18:48.480
Mile!

00:18:54.130 --> 00:18:56.030
M-Mile?

00:19:00.520 --> 00:19:02.240
Dad...

00:19:07.300 --> 00:19:10.000
Blaze brightly, righteous fires of hell!

00:19:10.000 --> 00:19:12.500
Burn them to ash!

00:19:15.740 --> 00:19:17.060
That's pointless!

00:19:17.060 --> 00:19:21.180
No matter how hot the flames, 
my KaBoom will not be burned.

00:19:26.060 --> 00:19:29.060
How foolish. It's your 
turn to fall into hell!

00:19:30.940 --> 00:19:31.900
Reina!

00:19:34.520 --> 00:19:36.270
Lattice Energy Barrier!

00:19:39.960 --> 00:19:41.590
Oh, it broke.

00:19:42.720 --> 00:19:43.620
Mile?!

00:19:43.820 --> 00:19:44.870
It can't be!

00:19:44.870 --> 00:19:46.620
You're still alive?

00:19:46.620 --> 00:19:50.090
Um... Oh, I thought I was gonna die!

00:19:51.040 --> 00:19:52.680
You impudent little...!

00:19:52.680 --> 00:19:55.270
This time I will send you to the next world!

00:19:55.270 --> 00:19:57.500
No, thank you.

00:19:55.270 --> 00:19:57.500
Huh? Wait! Wha?

00:19:58.190 --> 00:20:00.760
<i>I've had it with reincarnation already.</i>

00:20:00.960 --> 00:20:03.180
Ultra Freeze!

00:20:07.680 --> 00:20:11.140
Pointless! Pointless! 
You think that magic will work?

00:20:13.920 --> 00:20:15.270
It can't be...

00:20:15.270 --> 00:20:17.650
KaBoom's armor... How?

00:20:18.040 --> 00:20:19.360
Allow me to explain!

00:20:19.920 --> 00:20:21.610
No matter how strong the armor,

00:20:21.610 --> 00:20:24.180
if you raise it to a high temperature,
 then suddenly cool it,

00:20:24.180 --> 00:20:25.200
it becomes brittle.

00:20:27.390 --> 00:20:29.440
Well, you see it happen all the time.

00:20:30.160 --> 00:20:31.280
Which is why...

00:20:31.750 --> 00:20:32.960
This'll finish it!

00:20:41.510 --> 00:20:42.910
You did it, Mile!

00:20:45.280 --> 00:20:46.720
That was close.

00:20:46.720 --> 00:20:47.930
I'm glad it worked out.

00:20:50.200 --> 00:20:52.720
Man, look at the mess I made...

00:20:52.720 --> 00:20:54.690
I completely misjudged this.

00:20:54.960 --> 00:20:58.940
I thought I'd be able to sell you 
pretty girls for a high price.

00:20:58.940 --> 00:21:03.280
I'll sell you to a master 
who'll take good care of you.

00:21:08.580 --> 00:21:09.580
Reina-san?

00:21:10.920 --> 00:21:11.830
What are you doing?

00:21:11.830 --> 00:21:13.990
Roaring flames of ultimate fire!

00:21:13.990 --> 00:21:16.020
Enshroud and burn my enemy to ash!

00:21:16.750 --> 00:21:17.980
Hellfi—

00:21:17.980 --> 00:21:19.780
Don't, Reina-san!

00:21:20.760 --> 00:21:22.360
Stop, Reina!

00:21:22.360 --> 00:21:23.850
If you use that spell...

00:21:23.850 --> 00:21:26.660
Even his bones will melt!

00:21:31.880 --> 00:21:34.350
Guys! Get him!

00:21:34.350 --> 00:21:37.250
Tie him up! Stay still, damn it!

00:21:38.260 --> 00:21:40.820
Honestly! What were you thinking?

00:21:41.200 --> 00:21:42.480
Were you going to kill him?

00:21:49.720 --> 00:21:50.780
All of you...

00:21:53.050 --> 00:21:53.980
Have you...

00:21:55.260 --> 00:21:57.190
Have you ever killed anyone?

00:21:58.020 --> 00:21:58.690
What?
